---
title: Stir-fried Spinach (Qing Chao Bo Cai 清炒菠菜)
description: A minimalist approach to cooking spinach that highlights its natural flavor, enhanced simply with garlic and high heat.
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 2 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - spinach
  - vegetable
  - quick
  - chinese
  - side
cuisine: Chinese
course: Side
---

> Spinach cooks down incredibly fast and can easily become mushy. Keep the heat high and the cooking time short.

== Prepare Ingredients ==

Wash the @fresh spinach{300%g} thoroughly in several changes of water to remove any grit. If the stems are long, cut the spinach in half. Drain very well.

Smash and peel the @garlic{3%cloves}. You can leave them whole or roughly chop them.

== Stir-fry ==

Heat a #wok{} over medium-high heat. Add @neutral oil{1.5%tbsp}.

Add the smashed garlic and fry for ~{15%seconds} until fragrant and slightly golden.

Turn the heat to high. Add the drained spinach. It will seem like a lot but will shrink drastically.

== Season and Finish ==

Toss the spinach continuously. As soon as it starts to wilt (about ~{30%seconds}), add:
- @salt{¼%tsp}
- @chicken bouillon powder{¼%tsp} (optional)

Continue to toss for another ~{30%seconds} until the spinach is fully wilted but still bright green. Do not overcook or it will release too much water and turn mushy.

Serve immediately, leaving any excess liquid behind in the wok.